WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
We are all moving through spirals,

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:06.240
whether we like it or not, constantly

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.560
going up and down in frequencies. Some

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.920
people are caught in downward spirals,

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:12.880
replaying the same fears, same habits,

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:15.080
and emotional patterns all on a loop.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:16.760
They react the same way to the same

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:18.200
types of chaos, and they have the same

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.600
kinds of relationships, but with

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.320
different people all through their

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.560
lives. They think life is happening to

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:25.520
them, when ultimately they're the ones

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:27.840
reinforcing their patterns over and over

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:29.720
again. Others spiral upwards. They start

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:31.840
noticing their patterns. They know when

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:33.640
to interrupt their autopilot mode. They

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:36.320
realize how their thoughts shape

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:38.920
perception, perception shapes decisions,

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:40.680
and decisions ultimately shape reality.

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:42.560
In psychology, this is called cognitive

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:44.360
mapping, but in spirituality, people

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:46.360
will call this a spiritual awakening.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:49.080
But in reality, it is their awareness

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:51.200
replacing unconscious repetition. So,

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:53.280
most of us were handed the same script

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:55.400
as children to protect ourselves. Fear

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:57.640
change, stay small, and repeat

00:00:55.400 --> 00:01:00.320
whatever's familiar to us, so we mistake

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:03.120
that familiarity for safety. Even when

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:04.720
that familiarity is also destroying us.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:06.200
But the moment you realize you're not

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:07.600
just your shell, you're also the

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:09.520
controller, everything is going to

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:11.120
change. Your reality will reorganize

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:13.280
itself around the level that you choose

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:15.600
to operate from. So, this is why two

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:17.440
people can live in the exact same world

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:18.880
and still experience completely

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:20.680
different realities. One person

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:23.120
spiraling downwards into fear,

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:25.760
avoidance, and stagnation, and the other

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:28.080
is spiraling upward into awareness,

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:29.960
resilience, expansion. So, the only

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:31.840
question is, which direction are you

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:33.840
spiraling in? My name is Mae. This is

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:35.720
Stoic Angels. We're here to level up our

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:37.080
bodies, our mind, and our spirits. If

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:38.800
this is what you'd like to see more of,

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:40.920
subscribe to the channel and join the

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:42.920
family. The beauty of it all is

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:45.680
ultimately we're in control, and how we

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:47.320
react to life is still up to us despite

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:49.480
life happening to us, because our

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:52.760
reality is all about us reflected

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:55.120
outwards. Part one, our body is the key.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:57.720
So, let's talk about what actually makes

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:59.560
a spiral go up instead of down. Think

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:01.280
about the cycle of samsara in dharmic

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:03.320
philosophy, for example. By the way,

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:04.960
this is an extremely reductive and

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:06.440
simplified way to think about it, but it

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:08.399
helps us see things more clearly. The

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:10.840
definition of samsara itself is

00:02:08.399 --> 00:02:12.600
perpetual wandering, cause and effect, a

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:15.440
continuous flow of life, death, and

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:17.920
rebirth. It's really about karma. Karma

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:20.160
perpetuates samsara. We are all in the

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:22.560
cycle, all of us, nobody's exempt. If we

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:25.040
can break out of this karmic cycle, we

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:26.720
will achieve some form of enlightenment.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:29.280
But it all starts with yearning. Our

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:31.640
hopes, our dreams, a desire, then we

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:33.440
take action on it. We try to actualize

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:36.520
things through that action, which is how

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:38.320
we manifest our reality. Now, sometimes

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:41.120
things that we don't want happens to us,

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:43.240
which crushes us. We feel drained, we

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:45.640
feel like failures, and we react to that

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:48.400
reality with our feelings, then the

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:51.520
cycle repeats itself, but this time we

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:54.760
attach the pain of that failure with us.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:56.400
This becomes a downward spiral. Now, we

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:59.200
can't stop our yearning. That's

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:01.720
unrealistic, and desire is a part of the

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:04.080
human condition. But imagine if we can

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:06.320
detach our feelings from our desires.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:08.920
That is one good step forward. But many

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:10.720
of us were constantly reliving the

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:12.880
moments that make us feel a certain way.

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:15.640
For example, we rewatch TV shows,

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:17.560
movies, we replay scenarios in our head.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:19.600
Take this TikTok as an example. When

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:21.680
they already said good night, but you go

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:23.280
back to read the conversation to relive

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:25.000
the moment again. This is something

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:26.680
that's actually well documented by

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:28.720
systematic therapists working with

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:30.080
high-functioning clients. The people who

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:31.600
couldn't change their circumstances

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:34.280
weren't thinking negatively, but they

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:36.400
were actually thinking constantly to the

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:39.000
point where they can't stop. They start

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:41.040
to ruminate and obsess, which becomes

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:42.880
destructive for these high-functioning

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:44.920
people, and I suspect a lot of

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:47.040
incredibly smart people go through this.

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:49.400
Their enemy is actually their mind,

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:51.840
because past a certain point, the

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:54.280
analytical thinking and the logic turns

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:56.200
into an undesirable attachment and it

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:58.520
stops them from achieving their

00:03:56.200 --> 00:04:00.720
potential. When we're attached like

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:03.920
this, we're actually feeding our egos.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:07.120
Our egos want us to remain in the cycle.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:09.040
So, imagine how powerful we'll be if we

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:11.600
use this to our advantage instead of

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:13.200
just trying to feel safe and reinforcing

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:15.000
the cycle that we're in. So, how do we

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:17.359
reinforce that awareness? Because for

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:19.600
many of us, we intellectualize our

00:04:17.359 --> 00:04:21.480
self-improvement. We want to be better.

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:23.240
We try to write our way into becoming

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:25.240
better, changing the way we think and

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:27.000
speak to ourselves. Our thoughts come

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:30.000
from the cortex of our brain, but our

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:32.520
behavior is actually controlled by early

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.200
childhood experiences of feeling

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:35.960
threatened, which then gets buried

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:38.360
within our subcortical structures, the

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:40.320
pathways that run in our head

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:42.640
subconsciously. They have been there for

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:44.960
most of our lives and these subconscious

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:47.200
feelings will then continue to follow us

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:49.520
and lead our consciousness. It does not

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:51.440
respond to new ways of thinking, but

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:53.960
actually responds to our repeated

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:56.120
feelings over time. So, our emotions are

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:57.480
the key. When someone tells you to just

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:59.240
change your perspective and change your

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:01.000
thoughts and only that, they're not

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:03.040
taking into account your lived

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:05.080
experiences and the feelings that our

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:07.800
bodies have already been used to our

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:10.080
entire lives. Our body keeps the score,

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:11.640
which is a great book by the way. I just

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.600
finished it. I'll link it in description

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:15.400
as well. Like sure, your brain can think

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:16.840
new thoughts all you want. Eventually,

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:18.600
you may even affirm your way into

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:20.800
change, but your body needs to catch up,

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:24.040
too, and it can only catch up through

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:26.120
hundreds of repetitions of a new somatic

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:28.000
experience. Otherwise, it will continue

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:30.040
to feel these feelings of anxiety, of

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:32.320
fear, nervousness, which will keep you

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:33.960
small. For me, I think back on an

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:36.040
earlier time when I decided to be more

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:38.160
brave and confrontational and I want to

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:40.440
stand up for myself more. But, why did I

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:43.160
also break up in hives whenever I tried

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:44.720
to do that? It's because my body wasn't

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:47.080
used to me being brave and

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:48.920
confrontational. So, turns out you do

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:51.240
not just become what you think about,

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:53.880
you become what your nervous system has

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:56.600
learned to tolerate. This is why just

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:58.280
knowing alone does not produce change.

00:05:56.600 --> 00:06:00.880
Once you fully understand the role that

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:02.320
your body and your emotions also play in

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:04.080
it. This is that awareness that I'm

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:06.520
talking about, by the way. We will then

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:08.520
understand exactly where our upward

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:10.040
spiral can enter. Then you realize

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:12.880
people will find all kinds of ways to

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:15.120
unconsciously recreate the conditions of

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:16.560
your original early childhood wounds.

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:18.919
Because that familiarity makes them

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:20.480
think that it is safe even when it's

00:06:18.919 --> 00:06:22.200
destructive. They will do mental

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:23.640
gymnastics just to hold on to all of

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:25.640
these feelings. So, I'm going to be

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:27.000
honest, I know exactly what both

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:29.040
directions of upward and downward

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:30.600
spiraling feels like. So, I want to show

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:33.280
you something. This was me when I was a

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:36.600
teenager, and the only safe space she

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:38.840
had was in libraries reading books. Like

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:40.520
because home and school was not safe for

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:42.760
her. I look back at this version of

00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:44.720
myself and I feel so much tenderness and

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:47.360
love for her. That version of me feeling

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:49.000
safe in books still lives on today. And

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:50.720
this was also the time when I used to

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:52.560
romanticize the downward spiral to the

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:53.919
point where one of my favorite albums

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:55.760
when I was younger was called The

00:06:53.919 --> 00:06:57.840
Downward Spiral. I really identify with

00:06:55.760 --> 00:07:00.360
that because the sadness and the chaos

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:02.400
of the music felt at home to me and I

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:04.760
felt seen. It really spoke to me, but

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:06.600
that identification also kept me

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:08.760
trapped, too. When I was young, my

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:11.360
parents had violent fights every few

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:12.840
days. Sometimes it got so violent, I

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:14.440
thought someone's life was going to end.

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:17.120
A few times I even had to call the

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:18.960
police to make it stop. So, ultimately,

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:21.360
I escaped that situation as soon as I

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:24.040
could both metaphorically and literally,

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:26.000
but then it followed me, too, all

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:28.320
throughout my life. Turns out

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:30.040
unconsciously, I ended up seeking more

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:32.040
of these types of relationship drama

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:33.800
because of how it was normalized to me.

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:35.840
So, I am grateful to have been in

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:38.240
therapy as long as I have because

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:40.760
awareness is truly the first step to

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:42.560
fully and permanently breaking out of

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:45.240
these patterns. Once I was able to

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:46.920
realize how and why my past choices also

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:48.800
led to relationships that were also

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:50.400
violent and dramatic, I was able to

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:51.960
break out of it, which then led me to

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:53.680
the love of my life. And this year,

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:55.920
we've been married for 10 years, and

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:57.920
none of that drama exists today. Therapy

00:07:55.920 --> 00:07:59.960
helps you honor both truths at once.

00:07:57.920 --> 00:08:01.640
That version of you who was doing her

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:03.440
best with what she knew at the time, but

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:05.160
also you don't have to be trapped and

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:06.760
spiral even further. So, if you've been

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:08.760
wanting to start therapy, but the

00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:10.160
process feels overwhelming, BetterHelp,

