did to heal from these patterns, because

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:41.280
they helped me stop romanticizing things

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:43.039
I wanted good for me, and I was able to

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:45.320
come to the realization that I truly

00:08:43.039 --> 00:08:47.839
deserved better than that. Part two,

00:08:45.320 --> 00:08:49.480
reframing. How to change the direction.

00:08:47.839 --> 00:08:51.400
For the longest time, especially when I

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:52.839
was younger and I was rebellious kid, I

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:54.200
thought I wanted chaos to have an

00:08:52.839 --> 00:08:56.440
interesting life. I thought I could keep

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:58.480
doubling down on it, but that impulse

00:08:56.440 --> 00:09:00.520
ultimately still came from a place where

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:02.680
I didn't believe I deserved a chance to

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:04.080
succeed. I wasn't being badass or brave

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:06.440
just for the sake of it, but this was a

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:08.000
coping mechanism that I adopted as a

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:10.000
personality trait. And here's what I

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:11.760
learned about reframing that ultimately

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:13.760
changed everything for me. Your mind

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:16.040
only cares about the words that you feed

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:17.680
it, and you have to feel these words in

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:19.880
order to believe it. So, the more

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:22.000
negativity you repeat to yourself, the

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:23.520
more you talk down on yourself, the more

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:25.800
you will believe it to be true, and

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:27.720
eventually it will control you, because

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:29.839
you feel the effects from that, and you

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:31.920
reinforce it. Just like how music

00:09:29.839 --> 00:09:34.040
reinforced those beliefs for me that I

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:35.880
was ultimately not deserving of

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:38.520
happiness. And not only did I like the

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:40.200
music, I felt that with my soul. I look

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:42.040
at the tracklist of that album now that

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:44.840
I'm older and wiser and I see these

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:47.320
themes of hurt, dehumanization,

00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:50.200
self-destruction, sickness. Don't get me

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:52.800
wrong, like this is art. Art is supposed

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:54.240
to help people feel seen, to feel like

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:56.040
we're not alone, and to help us

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:58.160
understand new perspectives that we're

00:09:56.040 --> 00:10:00.600
not familiar with. And I still love this

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:02.560
album, but now that I see it with fresh

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:05.160
new eyes, I see the amount of pain that

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:07.000
I was in my younger self. So, it's

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:09.480
important to realize that and also be

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:12.040
able to see the words that people around

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:14.720
you are repeating to you and to one

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:17.200
another. Are they ultimately positive or

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:19.280
negative or are they affirming a stance

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:21.520
that you want to stay in even if it's

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:23.120
not good for you? Think about Sisyphus

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:25.440
in Greek mythology, the man who was

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:27.400
condemned to push a boulder uphill for

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:29.280
eternity and watch it roll back down

00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:31.720
every time. Albert Camus, a famous

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:34.480
philosopher, wrote that we must imagine

00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:36.600
Sisyphus happy. This means the point

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:39.120
isn't to escape the cycle, but to find

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:41.520
agency within it. That is how we

00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:43.120
so-called escape the cycle. Now, imagine

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:45.360
we are all Sisyphus, right? The downward

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:46.960
spiral is Sisyphus without awareness,

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:48.640
but the upward spiral is what happens

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:51.080
when you stop pushing this boulder up

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:52.560
the same hill, step back, and realize we

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:54.760
can choose a different mountain

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:56.680
entirely. Can we choose not to push the

00:10:54.760 --> 00:10:59.080
boulder? No, that's a part of life, but

00:10:56.680 --> 00:11:00.520
luckily for us, it all works the other

00:10:59.080 --> 00:11:02.720
way too. You can talk yourself into

00:11:00.520 --> 00:11:04.360
success with the same mechanism. And

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:06.400
this is not about wishful thinking

00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:09.000
because high-performing athletes do this

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:11.240
constantly. Michael Phelps, who by the

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:13.920
way shared the same birthday as me, fun

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:17.440
fact, he is the most decorated Olympian

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:19.520
in history with 23 gold medals. He uses

00:11:17.440 --> 00:11:21.560
a visualization and self-talk practice

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:23.240
before every single race, but here's

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:25.520
what made his approach different from

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:27.240
standard positive thinking. He didn't

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:29.720
just visualize winning. He actually

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:30.839
visualized disaster. Phelps discusses

00:11:29.720 --> 00:11:32.760
this method in detail in his

00:11:30.839 --> 00:11:34.680
autobiography, No Limits: The Will to

00:11:32.760 --> 00:11:36.640
Succeed, and in various interviews about

00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:38.880
his mental preparation with his coach,

00:11:36.640 --> 00:11:40.800
Bob Bowman. What happened is he would

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:42.880
visualize his goggles filling up with

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:44.960
water, getting disqualified, and coming

00:11:42.880 --> 00:11:47.400
in last. He then trained his nervous

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:49.560
system to stay calm and stable under any

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:52.000
condition, so when his goggles actually

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:53.960
did fill with water during the 200 meter

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:56.840
butterfly final at the 2008 Beijing

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:59.240
Olympics, he didn't panic. He won gold

00:11:56.840 --> 00:12:01.680
anyway, swimming the final 100 meters

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:03.640
essentially blind because his body had

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:05.200
already rehearsed the exact same

00:12:03.640 --> 00:12:07.520
scenario, and he knew how to deal with

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:10.000
it. Kobe Bryant is another famous

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:12.080
athlete who built his entire competitive

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:13.960
identity around internal awareness. He

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:16.400
called it the Mamba mentality, but at

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:17.920
its root, it was a self-talk system. He

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:19.680
said the key to everything was being

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:21.560
aware of how you're feeling and how you

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:23.280
need to be feeling, and that all starts

00:12:21.560 --> 00:12:25.200
with awareness. Before games, while

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:27.320
20,000 fans are screaming in an arena,

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:29.320
none of it moved him or affected him

00:12:27.320 --> 00:12:31.520
because he had already built a calm

00:12:29.320 --> 00:12:33.840
internal state before he even walks into

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:35.920
this arena. That is him practicing his

00:12:33.840 --> 00:12:38.240
learned nervous system response. Serena

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:40.480
Williams credits her mental game as much

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:42.120
as her physical ability for her 23 Grand

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:43.839
Slam singles title. She has spoken

00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:45.400
openly about using self-talk during

00:12:43.839 --> 00:12:48.080
matches, and one of the statements that

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:51.160
she's made publicly is, "I am powerful.

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:53.720
I am strong. I am worthy." That is her

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:55.800
deliberately rewiring her internal

00:12:53.720 --> 00:12:58.839
dialogue under intense competitive

00:12:55.800 --> 00:13:01.280
pressure. Naturally, research also backs

00:12:58.839 --> 00:13:04.120
all of this up. I found a 2019 published

00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:06.320
in Sports MDPI by Walter Nickel Isaac

00:13:04.120 --> 00:13:09.000
and Auffermann at Leipzig University,

00:13:06.320 --> 00:13:10.839
and they studied 111 junior sub-elite

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:12.839
athletes, and they found that structured

00:13:10.839 --> 00:13:15.280
self-talk training led to decreased

00:13:12.839 --> 00:13:17.680
anxiety, increased self-confidence,

00:13:15.280 --> 00:13:19.440
improved self-efficacy, and better

00:13:17.680 --> 00:13:21.280
performance ratings. Athletes who

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:23.920
trained self-talk for 8 weeks showed

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:26.040
significantly higher effects than those

00:13:23.920 --> 00:13:28.000
who only trained for 1 week. This means

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:30.320
how long you've been doing this practice

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:33.080
also matters. It is not like a one-time

00:13:30.320 --> 00:13:35.280
mindset shift, but a repeated somatic

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:37.400
and cognitive process that gets better

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:39.920
over time. In another study I found from

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:41.640
2002, psychologist Barbara Fredrickson

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:43.920
and Thomas Joiner published this

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:45.480
foundational study in Psychological

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:47.440
Science that demonstrated what they

00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:49.800
called the broaden and build theory.

00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:50.920
They found that positive emotions don't

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:52.720
just feel good in the moment, they

00:13:50.920 --> 00:13:55.000
actually broaden your cognitive

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:56.600
repertoire. Meaning positive emotions

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:58.600
actually extend the range of thoughts

00:13:56.600 --> 00:14:00.800
and actions that you can process, which

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:02.480
then builds personal resources like

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:04.920
resilience, social connection,

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:07.120
problem-solving capacity. And these

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:08.920
resources then generate even more

00:14:07.120 --> 00:14:11.280
positive emotions, creating what's

00:14:08.920 --> 00:14:13.760
literally an upward spiral and builds

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:16.000
natural confidence. So, the opposite is

00:14:13.760 --> 00:14:18.200
also true, of course. Negative self-talk

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:20.640
narrows your perception. It locks you

00:14:18.200 --> 00:14:22.720
into constantly feeling threatened. Your

00:14:20.640 --> 00:14:24.040
world gets smaller, your options shrink.

00:14:22.720 --> 00:14:26.440
You make the same decisions from the

00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:29.560
same contracted state, and the spiral

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:31.560
continues to go down. So, when I say you

00:14:29.560 --> 00:14:33.680
can talk yourself into success, I'm not

00:14:31.560 --> 00:14:35.640
saying just think positive. No, I'm

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:37.280
saying the words you use with yourself

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:38.880
literally shapes your brain. They also

00:14:37.280 --> 00:14:41.920
will eventually change what your nervous

00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:43.960
system considers safe. They change the

00:14:41.920 --> 00:14:46.040
way that you feel about situations and

00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:47.880
naturally what your perception allows

00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:50.520
you to notice. It is all about

00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:52.440
broadening your perception. Over time,

00:14:50.520 --> 00:14:54.760
they also change the direction of your

00:14:52.440 --> 00:14:56.480
spiral. Part three, the direction is

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:58.080
yours. So far, here are all the

00:14:56.480 --> 00:14:59.280
takeaways. The spiral is not something

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:01.040
that happens to you, it is something

00:14:59.280 --> 00:15:02.760
that you actively participate in whether

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:04.720
you're aware of it or not. We are all

00:15:02.760 --> 00:15:06.160
constantly spiraling in one way or

00:15:04.720 --> 00:15:07.600
another. Every thought that you repeat

00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:08.920
is also a vote in the direction that

00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:11.200
you're moving in. Everything that you

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:13.040
tolerate is also a vote. Every memory

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:14.800
that you replay in your head ends up

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:16.160
shaping your next decision because that

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:18.240
is what you're repeating to yourself.

00:15:16.160 --> 00:15:20.920
This is why I'm building a library of

00:15:18.240 --> 00:15:22.720
somatic exercises and meditations in my

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:24.280
Stoic Angels membership platform to

00:15:22.720 --> 00:15:26.480
rewire those negative thoughts that we

00:15:24.280 --> 00:15:29.280
have and help us focus on ourselves even

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:31.120
more, particularly and especially in our

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:32.240
upward growth. So, if you're interested,

00:15:31.120 --> 00:15:34.200
you can join the waitlist in my

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:35.760
description box and I will email you

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:38.120
when it's ready. I'm working on it right

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:40.080
now. But, there's so many studies behind

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:41.720
this. For example, reinforcing positive

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:43.720
emotions broaden your cognitive

00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:46.160
capacity. It builds better psychological

00:15:43.720 --> 00:15:48.480
resources for yourself. Self-talk, when

00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:50.640
practiced consistently, rewires our

00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:52.280
anxiety into self-confidence. And it's

00:15:50.640 --> 00:15:54.720
not just talk alone but the nervous

00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:56.520
system. While sure, it's slow to update

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:57.960
and it needs time to catch up, it does

00:15:56.520 --> 00:16:00.560
eventually update when you give it

00:15:57.960 --> 00:16:02.240
enough new evidence and reinforce that

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:03.760
constantly. You don't need to overhaul

00:16:02.240 --> 00:16:05.480
your entire life in a day. In fact,

00:16:03.760 --> 00:16:07.000
that's actually impossible. We still

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:08.440
want to be realistic, right? So, in the

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:10.280
meantime, you need to focus on

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:11.920
interrupting that loop and notice the

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:13.600
pattern as they come up. Choosing a

00:16:11.920 --> 00:16:14.880
different word to describe a situation,

00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:16.800
for example, that's a great way to

00:16:14.880 --> 00:16:18.880
reframe things because our language

00:16:16.800 --> 00:16:20.520
shapes our lives. Or, you can get used

00:16:18.880 --> 00:16:21.720
to being uncomfortable so that we can

00:16:20.520 --> 00:16:23.200
handle things better and then do it

00:16:21.720 --> 00:16:25.640
again tomorrow and then again the next

00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:27.720
day. That is how a spiral changes

00:16:25.640 --> 00:16:29.200
direction. So, if this resonated with

